 "lines": [
  "The cables snapped on floor eighty.",
  "Midnight. Kai, Leo and Mia, riding down alone.",
  "A bang. Then the floor dropped away.",
  "@am_echo: \"I'll jump right before we hit!\"",
  "@af_heart: \"That barely helps, Leo.\"",
  "From a hundred sixty-five feet, a perfect jump only slows you from seventy-two to sixty-five miles an hour.",
  "But elevators hide a speed sensor called a governor.",
  "Too fast, and its spinning weights fly out and lock.",
  "That trips the safety brakes. Steel jaws grab the rails.",
  "With a shriek of metal, they stopped.",
  "@af_heart: \"Elevators hang on several cables. Far more than they need.\"",
  "Otis proved it in [1854](eighteen fifty-four). He had his own elevator's rope cut. It held.",
  "@am_echo: \"Has anyone ever fallen all the way?\"",
  "@af_heart: \"Yes. And she lived.\"",
  "July [1945](nineteen forty-five). In thick fog, a bomber hit the Empire State Building.",
  "Elevator operator Betty Lou Oliver, twenty, was hurt on floor eighty.",
  "Rescuers sent her down in an elevator. Its damaged cables snapped.",
  "She fell seventy-five stories. Over a thousand feet.",
  "Squeezed air in the shaft likely slowed her. The coiled cables below cushioned her like a spring.",
  "She broke her neck, back and pelvis, and lived. Still a Guinness world [record](rekkerd).",
  "@am_michael: \"Okay. I'm taking the stairs.\"",
  "Because nobody wants to hear the cables snap on floor eighty."
 ],
